      "rev_n_22_ed980a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_22_ed980a_0",
        "node_id": "n_22_ed980a",
        "thought_text": "The current approach initializes the dp array with infinity values except for dp[0], which is set to 0. It then iterates through all possible pairs (i, j) where i > j to update the dp array with the minimum cost to complete the i-th task. However, the final result should be the sum of the costs to complete each task in an optimal sequence, not just the minimum value in the dp array.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4326946065134897702",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500580.3070073
      },
      "rev_n_23_e628fc_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_23_e628fc_0",
        "node_id": "n_23_e628fc",
        "thought_text": "The issue might lie in how the dp array is being updated. Instead of directly updating dp[i] with the minimum cost, it should accumulate the costs for each task completion. This means that for each task, the cost to complete it should be added to the accumulated cost of completing the previous tasks.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4326946065134897702",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500580.307035
      },
      "rev_n_24_f87b6c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_24_f87b6c_0",
        "node_id": "n_24_f87b6c",
        "thought_text": "Another potential issue could be the way the loops are structured. The outer loop should iterate over all tasks, and the inner loop should iterate over all previous tasks to calculate the cost of completing the current task after the previous ones. The final result should be the sum of the accumulated costs for all tasks.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4326946065134897702",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500580.3070512
      },
      "rev_n_23_e628fc_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_23_e628fc_1",
        "node_id": "n_23_e628fc",
        "thought_text": "The issue lies in how the `dp` array is being updated. Instead of directly updating `dp[i]` with the minimum cost, it should accumulate the costs for each task completion. This means that for each task, the cost to complete it should be added to the accumulated cost of completing the previous tasks. Additionally, the initialization of the `dp` array should start with index 0 and size 4, and `dp[0]` should be initialized to 0 because the cost to complete the first task is 0.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4326946065134897702",
